# Forklift kit redesign: implementation outline

The forklift has four existing cosmetic fields. Two independent selections are needed for the overhead guard and the forks. Preserve the existing option IDs and treat older four-field forklift saves as stock for both new selections. Keep the additional fields forklift-specific in save, sync, ownership, purchase, preview, race and ghost paths; reject them on other vehicles. A server rollout must accompany a client rollout.

The following are design candidates, not implemented or approved assets. Each group has the original plus ten alternatives; the older IDs retain their meaning and ownership.

- Engine cover: Original; vented; ribbed; twin intake; pressed louvres; crossflow; centre spine; screened; twin exhaust vents; raised scoop; smooth industrial.
- Rear guard: Original; single bar; wraparound; twin bar; tubular hoop; stepped bumper; deep plate; corner guards; slotted panel; wide crossbar; racing diffuser.
- Wheels: Original; solid disc; bright ring; six spoke; three spoke; five spoke; eight spoke; turbine; perforated steel; deep dish; split spoke.
- Side guards: Original; single rail; side plate; twin rail; tubular cage; stepped guard; ribbed plate; angled rail; recessed channel; modular blocks; wraparound guard.
- Driver frame: Original; reinforced; open tubular; cross-braced; double rail; curved roof; slatted roof; narrow pillars; heavy industrial; rally cage; flat canopy. Retain lamps, mirrors and beacon mounts, and avoid covering the operator or obstructing the mast.
- Forks: Original; narrow tapered; broad tapered; reinforced; twin-rib; rounded tip; serrated edge; low-profile; heavy-duty; skid shoe; industrial striped. Fit the existing raised carriage and keep the fork attachment points and clearance consistent with the collision-independent vehicle presentation.

Implementation needs replacement assemblies rather than overlays where the new part would otherwise intersect stock geometry. Preview frames must remain editable while the physical mast, moving wheels and livery materials remain intact. Assess every option in front, rear, side, top and three-quarter views, with full and simplified geometry and both desktop renderers. Exercise selection, cancellation, equip, reload, reset, old-save migration, account sync, ownership, race and ghost construction. Confirm that the four existing stock appearances stay unchanged.
